course: dictionary
lesson: 7346
title: Platelets: tiny repair teams
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A platelet is a tiny piece in your blood. Its job is to help blood clot, which means go thick and sticky, so bleeding stops when you are cut. «When you graze your knee, platelets plug the wound» tells you what they do.
explain: The word is built from two parts: "plate" and "-let". The ending -let means small, so a platelet is a small plate. Think of it as a little patch that sticks over a gap. Check your meaning by swapping it in: «platelets help stop bleeding» still makes sense with "tiny pieces that help blood clot".
explain: Context clues show that platelets work in a team. «Blood has red cells that carry oxygen, white cells that fight germs, and platelets that help stop bleeding» lists platelets with other parts of blood, each with its own job. Hospitals even check a "platelet count", which tells doctors how many platelets are in your blood.
fact: A platelet is a tiny piece in your blood that helps it clot.
fact: Clot means go thick and sticky, so that bleeding stops.
fact: «Platelets stick together at the cut» to make a plug.
fact: Platelets work with «threads of fibrin» that make a net, and the net dries into a scab.
fact: «Platelet» is a noun: one platelet, many platelets.
exercise: «When you cut yourself, platelets stick together at the cut.» What do platelets do here? | They fight germs | They make the blood flow faster | *They help blood clot and stop the bleeding | They carry oxygen around the body
exercise: «Red cells carry oxygen, white cells fight germs, and platelets help stop bleeding.» Which blood part helps stop bleeding? | White cells | Red cells | *Platelets | Skin
exercise: «Platelets plug the wound and threads of fibrin make a net that dries into a scab.» Which word is a noun for the dried crust over a cut? | *scab | plug | dries | net
test: A doctor checks a blood test for the number of platelets. What is this called? | Blood pressure cuff | Shoe size | *Platelet count | Heart rate
test: «Platelets help blood clot.» What does clot mean here? | Run very fast | Turn cold | *Go thick and sticky | Turn into bone
exam: Which is the best meaning of platelet? | A type of hot drink | A large bone in your leg | A germ that makes you ill | *A tiny piece in your blood that helps it clot
